attn-3 (docs/research/deepinfer/attention-kv.md, attn-3), mode E: int8-QK attention for KVarN's
chunked-prefill continuations, behind KVARN_PREFILL_INT8=1 (default unset = off, no code path changes).

KVarN's _cached_multiquery_path materialises the request's whole rotated fp16 K/V contiguously and runs FA2
varlen on it for every chunk after the first of a cold prefill (the fused verify kernel takes the short
verify steps first, so this branch only sees chunked-prefill continuations and shallow verifies). With the
knob, a one-request call with more than 16 query tokens at head_dim 256 runs the new
kvarn_prefill_int8.prefill_attn_int8_contig on the same q_rot / K_packed / V_packed instead: the
SageAttention-style kernel of patches/prefill-attn-int8.patch (K mean-smoothed, int8 per 64 keys and head;
Q int8 per row; P.V in V's dtype, fp32 accumulate), with contiguous K/V addressing and P cast to fp16.
Anything else (several requests, verify-sized calls, non-causal) keeps FA2. The knob is read once at import
(os.environ); the branch is inside the opaque attention op, so the torch.compile cache is unaffected.

Test: bench/test_kvarn_int8qk.py (GPU; against an fp64 reference and FA2). Applies on the stock image.

Apply: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz 0 -d /app/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < attn3-kvarn-int8qk.patch

